sec.p:
For COCH, variants were retained if they met the following criteria:
Observed with fewer than 5 alleles in gnomAD;
Predicted to be pathogenic by at least one in silico tool among CADD (>20), PolyPhen-2, REVEL, AlphaMissense, or SpliceAI (score ≥ 0.10);
Not retained if only a low CADD score (<22) or only “possibly damaging” prediction by PolyPhen-2 was present, and no stronger evidence supported pathogenicity;
No other more plausible genetic cause of hearing loss was identified.

Future directions include:
Functional validation of novel COCH variants;
Longitudinal vestibular assessments in carriers, especially in pediatric cases;
COCH analysis in NGS panels even in case of early hearing loss onset;
Investigation of modifier genes or regulatory elements influencing phenotypic expression.
